6092440 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186049056 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186092440 #edb/ref 1050 540.0 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186092440 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "b0819913-0358-5916-b4f8-7f50eb841426" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186092883 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186091498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186092883 #edb/ref 1069 "q-8828" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186092883 #edb/ref 1071 "Given that $x_{1}$ and $x_{2}$ are the solutions to the equation $5\\sin x - 2\\cos x = 0$ for $0 \\le x < 2π$, what is the value of $x_{1} \\cdot x_{2}$, rounded to $1$ decimal place?\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186092883 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "41fbb86c-53b6-5410-a547-305f18db5384" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186092883 #edb/ref 1073 true #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186092888 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186357179 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186092888 #edb/ref 1069 "q-8876" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186092888 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186092888 #edb/ref 1071 "Given that ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ are the solutions of the equation $3\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=0$ for $-\\pi <x\\le \\pi ,$ what is the value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186092888 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "40bdf0c4-a9af-5a19-bf92-60c84db76070" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186092888 #edb/ref 1073 true #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186092888 #edb/ref 1074 "We divide both sides of the equation by $\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$ and use the identity $\\operatorname{tan}⁡x=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}.$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x & =0 \\\\ \\frac{3\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x} & =0 \\\\ \\frac{3\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}\\cancel{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}}{\\cancel{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}} & =0 \\\\ 3\\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}-\\sqrt{3} & =0 \\\\ 3\\operatorname{tan}⁡x-\\sqrt{3} & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we rearrange the equation and isolate $\\operatorname{tan}⁡x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3\\operatorname{tan}⁡x-\\sqrt{3} & =0 \\\\ 3\\operatorname{tan}⁡x & =\\sqrt{3} \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡x & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3})=\\frac{\\pi }{6}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $\\frac{\\pi }{6}$ lies inside the given domain, our first solution is ${x}_{1}=\\frac{\\pi }{6}.$\n\nTo find the other solution, we subtract $\\pi $ from the principal value. Hence,\n\n$$\n{x}_{2}=\\frac{\\pi }{6}-\\pi =-\\frac{5\\pi }{6}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions are $x=-\\frac{5\\pi }{6},\\,\\frac{\\pi }{6}.$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}=-\\frac{5\\pi }{6}\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{6}=-\\frac{5{\\pi }^{2}}{36}.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186093099 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186093101 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186093099 #edb/ref 1061 23179 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186093099 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "5f21f197-7ffd-5a91-a7cf-62569b160ada" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186093099 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186093446 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186093101 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186093102 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186093101 #edb/ref 1061 23180 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186093101 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "8bdf2f12-06f6-5472-94cd-e7e7cf917e3b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186093101 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186092251 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186093102 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186093103 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186093102 #edb/ref 1061 23183 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186093102 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "efdc73f0-9d53-507a-a14e-a2410505fd66" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186093102 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186093447 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186093103 #edb/ref 1061 23185 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186093103 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "a1f55295-6e60-503c-aad2-f80f83e9b618" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186093103 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186092252 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186093446 #edb/ref 1064 "Suppose we want to find all of the solutions to the equation\n\n$$\n0\\le x<2\\pi .\n$$\n\nTo calculate a solution, we can reduce the equation to a more convenient form by dividing through by $\\cos x,$ and then use the identity $\\tan x = \\dfrac{\\sin x}{\\cos x}$ to simplify. This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}x-\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{cos}x & =0 \\\\ \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}x}{\\operatorname{cos}x}-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{cos}x}{\\operatorname{cos}x} & =0 \\\\ \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}x}{\\operatorname{cos}x}-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}\\cancel{\\operatorname{cos}x}}{\\cancel{\\operatorname{cos}x}} & =0 \\\\ \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}x}{\\operatorname{cos}x}-\\sqrt{3} & =0 \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}x-\\sqrt{3} & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we rearrange the equation and isolate $\\tan x\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\tan x = \\sqrt{3}\n$$\n\nWe can immediately calculate the principal value $x\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\nx = \\arctan(\\sqrt{3}) = \\dfrac{\\pi}{3}\n$$\n\nSince $\\dfrac{\\pi}{3}$ lies inside the given domain, our first solution is $x_1 = \\dfrac{\\pi}{3}.$\n\nTo find the other solution in the given interval, we add $\\pi\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} & ={x}_{1}+\\pi  \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{3}+\\pi  \\\\  & =\\frac{4\\pi }{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the solutions are $x = \\dfrac{\\pi}{3}, \\dfrac{4\\pi}{3}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186093446 #edb/ref 1065 3925 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186093446 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "e6a96a57-0e08-54b9-9ccf-a0facd4b8c41" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186093446 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186093447 #edb/ref 1064 "Let's find all the solutions to the equation\n\n$$\n-\\pi <x\\le \\pi .\n$$\n\nNotice that this time, the domain is $-\\pi <  x \\leq \\pi.$\n\nFirst, we divide each term of the equation by $\\cos x$ and use the identity $\\tan x = \\dfrac{\\sin x}{\\cos x}$ to simplify. This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}x-\\operatorname{cos}x & =0 \\\\ \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}x}{\\operatorname{cos}x}-\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}x}{\\operatorname{cos}x} & =0 \\\\ \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}x}{\\operatorname{cos}x}-\\frac{\\cancel{\\operatorname{cos}x}}{\\cancel{\\operatorname{cos}x}} & =0 \\\\ \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}x}{\\operatorname{cos}x}-1 & =0 \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}x-1 & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we rearrange the equation and isolate $\\tan x\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\tan x = 1\n$$\n\nWe can immediately calculate the principal value $x\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\nx =  \\arctan(1) = \\dfrac{\\pi}{4}\n$$\n\nSince $\\dfrac{\\pi}{4}$ lies inside the given domain, our first solution is $x_1 = \\dfrac{\\pi}{4}.$\n\nTo find the other solution in the given interval, we *subtract* $\\pi.$ Hence:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} & ={x}_{1}-\\pi  \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{4}-\\pi  \\\\  & =-\\frac{3\\pi }{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the solutions are $x = -\\dfrac{3\\pi}{4} , \\dfrac{\\pi}{4} .$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186093447 #edb/ref 1065 3926 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186093447 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "20a00eec-d00f-52e6-8e26-03eb611ec5fc" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186093447 #edb/ref 1067 "Solving Trigonometric Equations Using the Sin-Cos-Tan Identity Under a Modified Domain" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186354704 #edb/ref 1080 "-\\frac{{\\pi }^{2}}{4}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186354704 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186354704 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "05e2e080-3c1b-5c3d-826a-c4649c776f9a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186354975 #edb/ref 1080 "-\\frac{7{\\pi }^{2}}{36}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186354975 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186354975 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "25